Scott 1976, Theorem 7.2 (iii). For arbitrary elements, relatedness in E of a ⊗ b agrees with relatedness in the product of E_a and E_b.

A related pair in E of the product is one element of the product repeated. Theorem 4.4 (ii) splits it into a pair of typed components, and those typings are the two component relations. Conversely, the component relations give equal components and the typings, so the two pair equations force the elements to be equal, and Theorem 4.4 (ii) places each in the product.
